```python
def f(n):
    if n < 2:
        return n
    return f(n - 1) + 2 * f(n - 2)

print(f(5))
```

This Python 3 function intends to return the length of the longest substring without repeated characters, but the marked line is wrong. Which single replacement fixes it for every string?

```python
def longest_unique(s):
    last = {}
    left = best = 0
    for right, ch in enumerate(s):
        if ch in last:
            left = last[ch] + 1  # BUG
        last[ch] = right
        best = max(best, right - left + 1)
    return best
```
